                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I've played nearly all of the Nancy Drew games and although this one isn't in my top tier list, it's still fun. A rich and interesting setting combined with actual history helped me as a history nerd engage further with the story. The characters had a nice variety to them as well, no two were truly alike and I had fun getting to know them. The puzzles were challenging but fair for the most part. My biggest critique is one that I have for most of the ND games which is that sometimes it's quite hard to know what to do next because the story and/or hints aren't clear enough. I had to refer to a guide to know what to do next several times. But other than that, it was still a fun play.",
